keyswap for Debian
==================

keyswap installs:

- the executable Python daemon
- a fallback configuration in /etc/keyswap/config.json
- a systemd user unit: keyswap.service
- a udev rule for input access

Configuration precedence
------------------------

1. --config /path/to/config.json
2. ~/.config/keyswap/config.json
3. /etc/keyswap/config.json

First-time setup
----------------

If your user was not already in the required groups, add it and then log out and back in:

    sudo usermod -aG input,uinput "$USER"

Create your personal config:

    mkdir -p ~/.config/keyswap
    cp /etc/keyswap/config.json ~/.config/keyswap/config.json

Enable the user service:

    systemctl --user daemon-reload
    systemctl --user enable --now keyswap.service

Check logs:

    journalctl --user -u keyswap.service -f
